  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's round the number of laptops and tablets in store A:\n\n- Laptops: $72⟶70$\n\n- Tablets: $38⟶40$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of laptops to the number of tablets (expressed as a fraction) is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{70}{40}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the number of laptops and the denominator represents the number of tablets.\n\nDividing the numerator and denominator by $10$ gives an equivalent fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{70÷10}{40÷10}=\\frac{7}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can make a numerator of $35$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7\\times 5}{4\\times 5}=\\frac{35}{20}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $20$ tablets in store B.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
